{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And Terach took, etc.</b> The intent is along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Bava Metzia 75a): ״מַאן דְּבִישׁ לֵיהּ בְּהַאי מָתָא״ — and so forth, for a change of place brings about a change [of fortune]. Therefore Scripture says this, for when Terach saw that his son Abram had not been born children, he effected a change of place and took Abram and Sarai to bring them to another place. And Scripture further informs us in this that Abraham was so esteemed in their eyes that on his account his entire father's household traveled to change the place for his sake — and this is what it says: <b>and they went forth with them</b>."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:24.141908817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}